  "slug": "models-foundation-782d",
  "summary": "Nine preprints extend sequence foundation models to Plasmodium, methylation, ncRNA and lncRNA, with variant-effect diagnostics and generative regulatory DNA design.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is moving nucleic-acid foundation models from generic pretraining toward specialized inputs, objectives and uses. An apicomplexan model pretrained on 455 assemblies targets regulatory prediction in the data-sparse P. falciparum genome, and ModBERT adds population variants and long-read CpG methylation to pretraining. For RNA, B-RANKO (bidirectional decoder-only ncRNA), LncRFM (structure-guided masking, 24.7M sequences) and MARRI (opening penalties and hybridization gains) encode RNA-specific properties. Evaluation is diagnostic: LAMP links failed personal-genome fine-tuning to distal sequence, and Borzoi and AlphaGenome are compared with variant-based methods in admixed Latino individuals. GENECraft and REGAL use these models for controllable regulatory DNA and enhancer design, REGAL with cross-species validation. All nine are preprints, so the claims remain unreviewed.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
